  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "An error of \\(0.02''\\) is made in the measurement of a line \\(10''\\) long, while an error of only \\(0.2''\\) is made in a measurement of a line \\(100''\\) long. In comparison with the relative error of the first measurement, the relative error of the second measurement is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "Greater by \\(0.18\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "The same"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "Less"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(10\\) times as great"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "Correctly described by both \\((A)\\) and \\((D)\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1951-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The two relative errors are \\(\\frac{0.02}{10}=0.002\\) and \\(\\frac{0.2}{100}=0.002.\\) They are equal.\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Relative error is the absolute error divided by the measured length",
        "Compare \\(\\frac{0.02}{10}\\) with \\(\\frac{0.2}{100}\\)"
      ],
